ngs the best however by the end  of the anime the symbol that pops up is  an adult but rather to Kanji symbols  that sell child so we can take this to  mean the now that goes from trying to  act like an adult to realizing in the  end that being a child is better that  the adult world makes no sense and that  he shouldn't try to become one of them  that he shouldn't try to be trapped in  the box of the adult world  shout out to occupy us for making her  video on Easter eggs and fooly cooly and  I will leave the link to that video in  the description so why does all of this  matter why is fully Cooley such an  important anime it's because we right  now are living in this adult world we  live in a world where things like money  is all that matters where the truth can  be bought with that same money through  media propaganda and where those who are  already powerful get to decide what the  rest of us should and should not do as  anime fans how many times have we been  told to grow up to act our age to do  what everyone else wants us to do  instead of doing what makes us happy  when you are told to act your age what  you are really being told is to conform  to the rules and expectations of society  you are being told to stop being  creative and stop thinking outside the  box I recently saw a handout that is  being given to future high school  teachers by their university professors  and this handout featured an image that  warned students that they could lose a  potential job opportunity if they write  something inappropriate on social media  or if they make an embarrassing you  to video now of course we know that  sometimes people post ridiculous things  on social media and everyone should know  that when you post something publicly  it's going to stay public however what  this handout what this image is really  telling us is to conform to conform to  the rules and expectations of society to  conform to the rules and expectations of  some employer before we even get the